# The gift promised on a spell is promised on its copy too, to the same opponent (ruling 2024-07-26). Bot2 casts two
# Lightning Bolts at Bot1; Bot1's Bilbo's Gambit (gift promised) takes the first and Lutri, the Spellchaser copies it
# with the second Bolt as the copy's new target. The copy resolves first (the second Bolt returns, Bot2 creates a
# Treasure), then the original (the first Bolt returns, Bot2 creates another): two Treasures, both Bolts back in hand,
# and Bot1 undamaged. A copy is not cast, so Lutri's cast before either resolved is allowed; afterwards nobody can cast.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Bilbo's Gambit
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Plains x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bilbo's Gambit.Cast
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lutri, the Spellchaser.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
? Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Treasure Token
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Bilbo's Gambit
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Treasure Token; Treasure Token
Bot2.Hand = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt; Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains
